    "text": "I have chosen the evening science course. I want to learn more about the river near my home, and the curriculum includes a project about local water.\n\nNo, it is on Wednesday at seven. The adviser said the classroom is in the older building on campus, next to the library.\n\nWe will hear a short lecture about asking clear questions. Then we will have a seminar to discuss possible topics in small groups.\n\nPlease do. The teacher also offers a tutorial on Friday for students who need help with the assignment.\n\nA short report. First we plan to do research using the library's books. Then we decide what information belongs in the report.\n\nNot in the first week. Later, a biology teacher will show us how to observe water plants safely. A chemistry teacher will help another group.\n\nThe teacher recommends two short study periods a week. The final assessment is a project and a discussion, not a long examination.\n\nNo. A graduate I met said people with different levels of education are welcome. She also studied history and literature at the center.\n\nGreat. I will bring my notebook on Wednesday so we can compare ideas after the lecture.",
